Docker Compose

### 👟 Reproduction steps

### Reproduction steps

1. Set `UPTIME_KUMA_HIDE_LOG=warn_domain_expiry` in `.env` or Docker Compose environment.
2. Have any HTTP(s) monitor targeting a domain with an unsupported TLD (e.g. `.ch`, `.at`, `.me`).
3. Restart Uptime Kuma.
4. Observe that `[DOMAIN_EXPIRY] WARN:` messages still appear in the logs despite the hide rule.




### 👀 Expected behavior

### Expected behavior

`UPTIME_KUMA_HIDE_LOG=warn_domain_expiry` should suppress all WARN-level log entries from the `DOMAIN_EXPIRY` module, as documented in the wiki and code comments.



### 😓 Actual Behavior

### Actual behavior

The `UPTIME_KUMA_HIDE_LOG` variable has no effect on WARN (or INFO/ERROR) level messages. Only DEBUG-level filtering could theoretically work (in development mode), though this is untested.

